{
  "results": [
    {
      "n": "G1",
      "evidence": "All five screenshots show the 3D scene rendering in Chrome with no blank screen or errors.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G2",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2–5 confirm smooth camera orbiting and zooming around the stack, and OrbitControls sets maxPolarAngle to Math.PI * 0.465 and maxDistance to 15.5 so the camera stays above the cloth and within its 34x34 bounds.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G3",
      "evidence": "The scene uses around 45 meshes, one InstancedMesh, one Points cloud, two shadow maps, a transmission pass, and basic post-processing (Bloom and BokehPass), which is light enough to maintain 30+ fps on a typical laptop.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "1",
      "evidence": "All five screenshots display a bottom UI bar containing instructional text ('Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom') and two interactive buttons ('Macro DoF: ON' and 'Hero Angle').",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "2",
      "evidence": "Inspection of the animate() loop in the code shows it only updates camera controls, focus distance, and renders static meshes, with no environmental motion running.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "3",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 frames the French toast stack close up and centered on the plate from slightly above, matching the general camera angle and framing of the reference photo.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "4",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 show three thick slices stacked and rotated at slight offsets relative to one another.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "5",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show banana slices placed between the toast layers, on top of the stack, and on the plate to the left and front of the stack.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "6",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show a cluster of blueberries on top of the stack and several more arranged around the base on the plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "7",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show the stack resting on a dark round plate set atop a grey-brown cloth surface.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "8",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show white sugar particles distributed in arcs across the dark plate and lightly speckling the top toast slice and berries.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "9",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–5, the toast slices have uniform scalloped, wavy perimeters and smooth plastic-like surfaces that resemble molded biscuits rather than thick cut bread with natural crusts.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "10",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1 and 4, the visible banana slices are round discs displaying a faint brownish three-pointed seeded pattern at their centers.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "11",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show round blueberries of slightly varying sizes with recessed five-pointed crowns visible at their poles.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "12",
      "evidence": "In Screenshot 2, a blueberry under the middle toast slice hangs partially clipped in mid-air above the plate, and multiple fruit pieces intersect deeply rather than resting naturally on surfaces.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "13",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 2, 3, and 5 prominently expose the straight outer edge of the tablecloth against a black void, and Screenshots 1–4 show harsh circular crease lines on the plate and cutout-like intersections on the toast.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "14",
      "evidence": "In the code, keyLight is placed in front of the stack at (-5.2, 8.4, 5.4) casting shadows backward in Screenshot 5 rather than coming from behind and left, and the syrup lacks bright warm highlights in Screenshot 1.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "15",
      "evidence": "In Screenshot 1, despite BokehPass being enabled, the back rim of the plate and the far edge of the cloth remain nearly sharp instead of softly blurred as in the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "16",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1 and 4, the far-left banana slice and the blueberries on top of the stack lack soft contact shadows where they meet the plate and toast.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "17",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 has a solid pitch-black empty background strip across the top of the frame above the cloth horizon, and the outer shadow areas of the plate fall to near-complete black.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "18",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1, 3, and 5, the syrup drips on the crust and puddles on the plate look like dark, dull brown plastic ridges and opaque rust-colored patches rather than glossy translucent amber.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "19",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show smooth, evenly shaded yellow-and-orange surfaces on the toast with regular vertical grooves and no porous bread crumb texture.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "20",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the blueberries display high-contrast, blotchy marbled blue-and-black patterns with glossy clearcoat reflections instead of a soft, dusty matte bloom.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "21",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1, 3, and 4, the banana slices look flat, opaque, and greyish-white with dark Rim shading artifacts, showing neither moistness nor slight translucency.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "22",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–5, the tablecloth reads as a blurry grey-beige plaster or sand plane with no visible woven fabric structure, and the plate displays an artificial concentric ring artifact.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "23",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show both the plate and the tablecloth surface sitting horizontally level with no unintended tilt.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "24",
      "evidence": "In the HTML source, the syrup rivulets and puddles are static TubeGeometry and CylinderGeometry meshes with no animation in animate().",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "25",
      "evidence": "Neither the screenshots nor the HTML code contain any steam or warm haze particle effect.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "26",
      "evidence": "There is no environmental motion implemented anywhere in the scene's render loop.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "27",
      "evidence": "Each blueberry and banana slice in the code is generated with a distinct procedural deformation seed, radius, and 3D rotation, avoiding identical adjacent copies in Screenshots 1–4.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "28",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show severe clipping throughout the stack, with banana slices and blueberries sinking halfway into the toast meshes and intersecting the plate.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "29",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the sugar on the black plate appears as large, discrete white pellets and coarse dots rather than fine dusted powder.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "30",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 is immediately recognizable as stylized 3D graphics due to its scalloped plastic-like toast, blotchy berries, severe mesh clipping, coarse white dots, visible table edge, and UI overlay.",
      "pass": false
    }
  ]
}
